all right so you know your first year  when you're walking around with that  around your neck don't make that mistake  in this video i'm going to break down my  top seven back to school essentials as  well as my top five biggest waste of  money items always recommended to  architectural students in their first  years of university and college if you  stick around to the end of the video i'm  going to share with you my absolute  favorite item from this entire haul that  i still use today as a qualified  practicing architect that cost less than  forty dollars but let me be clear a back  to school architecture hall is  expensive i hope your piggy bank is full  because this isn't going to be cheap now  yes you can absolutely 100 cheap out but  don't forget architecture is a very long  degree and if you're going back to  school for architecture you don't want  to be buying things twice so let's start  off this video with my top five do not  buys it doesn't matter who tells you  what i guarantee you that all of these  items will collect dust very very  quickly the number one item on this list  is a portfolio bag i guarantee you that  any first year architecture student  walking across campus is carrying a  portfolio bag and at the same time i  guarantee you'll never use it yes they  might try and tempt you to use it in the  first couple of weeks just so you get  some value out of purchasing this couple  hundred dollar bag but in reality it's  gonna sit in the back of your cupboard  for five straight years while you go  through your entire degree so save your  money don't buy the portfolio bag next  on the list is a storage tube and yes  technically speaking every architect  depicted in every movie ever has some  sort of storage tube and is carrying  around hundreds of rolls of paper under  their arms but again in the modern day  and the modern age you hardly ever carry  around any papers yes i still do carry  around papers and yes you still will  carry around papers however one roll of  paper under your arm is absolutely fine  a little bit of water on it is never  actually going to happen and the reality  of you requiring a storage tube is so  low it is not worth the money at all so  on this list is extremely controversial  and i guarantee you everybody is going  to advise against it however in my  personal experience i went out and  bought every single architecture book  available on the recommended list that  set me back close to a thousand dollars  in my first year and what i found out is  that when you rock up to every single  class with all those books in your  backpack ready to go eager to learn not  one single time are you gonna have to  pull out 95 of those books my honest  opinion is go out to your first week of  classes cop the grunt that comes with it  by not having all of the recommended  books with you and then make sure you  purchase the ones that are 100 essential  you can find 90 of the information in a  second handbook or online for 100 free  so i don't think you need to spend all  of the money on all of the recommended  books second last on this list is copic  markers now unless you are already an  existing artist who knows what they're  doing  freehand sketching designing and  performing very well in 2d animations or  even 3d representations on a piece of  paper copic markers are going to be the  biggest waste of money yes they're  phenomenal as an architectural tool yes  you can create some amazing 2d  watercolor designs landscape  architecture elevations but if you don't  know how to freehand draw you're  absolutely wasting your money because  nowadays they don't teach you how to  draw in architecture school they teach  you how to design using digital software  and technology though unfortunately the  day of architects knowing how to draw  and being trained to draw is long gone  number five on the do not buy list and  the last one on this list is a personal  favorite of mine it is the t-square  there is absolutely no reason any  architecture student should still go  around carrying a t-square now let's  move on to the architecture essential  must buy haul list for all  back-to-school architecture students the  number one on this list is coffee now  you're going to need so much coffee to  get through architecture school because  if you don't pull an all-nighter have  you really gone to architecture school  whilst you're at a supermarket grabbing  your coffee you may as well move on to  number two and grab some baking paper  now traditionally speaking architects  use yellow tracing paper and this is  absurdly expensive it can be anywhere  from fifty dollars all the way up to a  couple hundred dollars for some tracing  paper what i learned very quickly as a  poor university student is go to the  local supermarket  get some non-greased baking paper for  one or two dollars and it is the perfect  tracing paper number three on this list  like i mentioned before is a digital  item it is something that you're going  to need to produce great quality work  and because nobody draws freehand  anymore that means you're going to be  using a computer 24 7 to do your work  you are going to need a good laptop at  architecture school regardless if you're  planning to work at home or at  university i do often recommend a pc  rather than a mac for all architecture  students going in because pcs cater to  all of the architectural software which  i talked about in my last video compared  to what mac is actually compatible with  so pc is by far the easiest choice if  you don't know what software you're  going to be using to pair with pc you're  going to need the perfect mouse carpal  tunnel is dead serious in architecture  and you're going to need an ergonomic  mouse i have two of my personal favorite  recommendations one is the mx logitech  master iii mouse which is the be all  end-all of all mice and it is something  that anybody will recommend to you for  anything however the second mouse that  i've personally found to be actually  extremely comfortable while sitting and  doing an absurd amount of work on the  computer is the kensington wireless  mouse for life now i have linked all of  these things down in the description  below if you want to check them out next  on the list is my absolute favorite  black book in the world this little  black book is a typical moleskine it is  a hardcover moleskine because as an  architecture student this is the one  thing that you need to carry around  everywhere without this moleskine book i  probably would have failed my degree i  probably would have forgotten every  single thing somebody taught me but i  used to go through about three to five  of these every single semester because  it was my bible now i recommend the  moleskine with the grid lines over any  of the other mole skins because it is  incredibly versatile you can do  everything from architectural drawing  through to some basic note taking on the  grids and the paper feels incredible  paired with a great fine liner now  because we do live in 2022 you can very  easily scrap the moleskin and buy  yourself a brand new ipad paired with an  apple pencil this thing will do  everything that a moleskin wheel except  that has a battery life personally i  used to go in with an ipad and then i'll  go back to my desktop at home to take  all my notes whilst i was at university  and actually do my work at home so i  never really had a great laptop that i  always took into university and then did  all of my work there because i didn't  see the value in it but if you're unlike  me and you do actually want to go to  university stay at the college campus  for as long as you possibly can and do  all of your studying in the dorm rooms  in the library or wherever you see fit  you're probably going to need a good set  of headphones and you're probably going  to want them to be noise cancelling as  well so a set of beats by dre will do  the job perfectly well as will some  apple airpods pro  but you will need a set of good  headphones to be able to drown out all  of the other students and basically stay  in your flow state for as long as  possible to do some of the best work for  prolonged periods of time especially at  a huge time crunch anyway that's all for  me today guys thank you so much for  watching my name is david thomas and if  you enjoyed the content and want to see  more of it there is a playlist to the  side of me with great architectural  information available for free and if  you really love the content i'd  appreciate it if you smash that  subscribe button but like always i'll  see you next monday

